{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Who created a client registration (D5, T21.4). The discriminator that separates a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"registration an administrator made from one that arrived over an open endpoint. Three things"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"read it and each would otherwise have to infer provenance from something that is not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"provenance: * "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"axiam_oauth2::fapi"},{"type":"text","text":" refuses a FAPI profile on anything but"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"Self::Admin","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" (I5) — a client nobody vetted cannot be financial-grade; * the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"authorization endpoint forces a consent hop for every other value (D4) — an unrelated party","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"gets a question put to the end user, whatever scopes it asked for; * the T21.4 sweeper","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"deletes only ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"Self::Dcr"},{"text":" rows, so an administrator’s client is never swept however","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"long it sits unused. ","type":"text"},{"overridingTitleInlineContent":[{"code":"Admin","type":"codeVoice"}],"isActive":true,"overridingTitle":"Admin","type":"reference","identifier":"Self::Admin"},{"text":" is the serde default and therefore what every","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"row written before T21.4 decodes to, which is the truth: they were all created through ","type":"text"},{"code":"POST \/oauth2-clients","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" by somebody holding ","type":"text"},{"code":"oauth2_clients:create","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"roleHeading":"Enume